{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ec66e52411ba563376289d729c0707d222b165e9b0fbaeb722b12c8be5b6acd1","digest":{"component_or_area":"metrics snapshot storage and retrieval","key_entities":["src/rebar/metrics/snapshot.py","write_snapshot","read_snapshots",".rebar/metrics-snapshots.ndjson",".gitignore","tests/unit/metrics/test_snapshot.py",".rebar/"],"problem_keywords":["metrics snapshot","ndjson","persistence","trend tracking","code health"],"propositions":["A new NDJSON snapshot file must be created and read to persist point-in-time code-health metrics (coverage, complexity, clone count) across CI runs.","The snapshot store must live at .rebar/metrics-snapshots.ndjson (a git-tracked path) and be explicitly un-ignored in .gitignore so the trend series accumulates durably.","The read_snapshots function must filter records by date range and skip malformed/truncated lines without raising an error, returning only valid records.","The write_snapshot function appends a timestamped JSON record to the NDJSON file, and round-trip read-after-write must return the written record within its date range."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787319029195872001,"uuid":"f4513067-271d-433b-93d1-ce23b9d9fcca"}